% The questions of LOMO's requirements document (its competency questions),
% as far as a description can answer them.
scenario description is, as stated in the source description:
    actions_of_rules expects answers ["description 1 produces item 1 action", "description 2 produces item 2 action", "description 3 produces action 2", "description 3 produces action 3", "description 3 produces item 3 action"].
    actions_of_agents expects answers ["beneficiaries programme desk acts as addresser in action 1", "european commission national authorities national agencies beneficiaries participants acts as addressee in item 1 action", "european commission national authorities national agencies beneficiaries participants acts as addressee in item 2 action", "european commission national authorities national europass centres european qualifications acts as addressee in item 3 action", "general publiccommissioneuropean parliamentcouncil of the european union acts as addressee in action 1", "individuals acts as addressee in action 2", "individuals acts as addresser in action 2", "national authorities acts as addresser in action 3", "national authorities education training providers individuals acts as addressee in action 3"].

query parts is:
    which thing is part of the description.

query kinds is:
    which thing is of the kind which kind.

query bearer is:
    the bearer role is which role.

query rules_of_act is:
    which rule is established by the act which act.

query provisions is:
    which thing is established in which provision.

query places is:
    which rule is laid down in which place.

query joint_rules is:
    which rule is established in more than one provision.

query prescriptive is:
    which thing is a prescriptive rule.

query constitutive is:
    which thing is a constitutive rule.

query triggers is:
    which thing is triggered by which event.

query actions_of_rules is:
    which rule produces which action.

query addressers is:
    which agent acts as addresser in which action.

query addressees is:
    which agent acts as addressee in which action.

